#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:11
#: 5bb534054f404ef28954e465aaf391a2
msgid ""
"The APM2.x is end of life for use with ArduPilot. This article is made "
"available for existing users."
msgstr "APM2.x 已停止与 ArduPilot 配合使用。本文仅供现有用户参考。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:14
#: c154b3e31684491da5fdbbdfc63afa76
msgid ""
"This article demonstrates the options for powering the APM2.x board along "
"with information about the requirements for connecting the power rail."
msgstr "本文介绍了 APM2.x 飞控板的供电选项，以及连接电源轨的相关要求。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:19
#: ba5f58edeb6a442f893612f22bbfd18d
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概述"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:21
#: 901f468160e64365b2b7374232273b3e
msgid ""
"Like any computer, the APM needs a power supply with a steady clean voltage "
"and sufficient current."
msgstr "与任何计算机一样，APM 需要稳定、纯净、足够电流的电源供应。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:24
#: 68d70b184f294b04ba8b61f0c018d0ce
msgid ""
"3DR provides an :ref:`3DR Power Module <common-3dr-power-module>` that "
"supplies 2.25A at 5.37V. The module is designed to convert power from the "
"main flight battery (18 Volt maximum).  That module will supply sufficient "
"power for your APM, and low power radios including your RC receiver (without"
" servos). Your RC receiver can be powered from any APM Input (+5V and "
"ground). This is normally done by connecting a 2 or 3 wire cable between an "
"APM Input and one of the output channels on the RC radio."
msgstr ""
"3DR 提供了一个 :ref:`3DR Power Module <common-3dr-power-module>`，可在 5.37V 下输出 "
"2.25A。该模块设计用于从主飞行电池（最高 18V）转换电源。该模块可为您的 APM "
"以及包括接收机在内的低功耗无线设备提供足够的电源（不含舵机）。您的接收机可从任意 APM 输入引脚（+5V 和地）取电，通常通过在 APM "
"输入端和遥控接收机某个输出通道之间连接一根 2 或 3 芯线缆来实现。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:33
#: ce6657da4cb649d3a8fbbdee2cc51a8d
msgid ""
"If you are using any servos such as are required with a traditional "
"helicopter or a camera gimbal, you will need to provide an additional "
"dedicated power supply for the servos. The APM is intended to **control** "
"servos, not power them."
msgstr "如果您使用了舵机（如传统直升机或云台摄像头所需），则需要为舵机提供专用的额外电源。APM 的作用是 **控制** 舵机，而不是为其供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:38
#: 3643d2a72b504198ae5bc5d1f66de3a5
msgid ""
"The following sections describe the APM power circuit (you will need to "
"understand this in order to design a power supply for your APM, or provide "
"additional power), and your options for powering the APM and connected "
"components."
msgstr ""
"以下各节介绍了 APM 的供电电路（您需要了解这些内容，以便为 APM 设计供电方案或提供额外电源），以及为 APM 及其连接组件供电的各种选项。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:44
#: 87b28eb4063447ca862d4cf1447e6f8c
msgid "APM power circuit"
msgstr "APM 供电电路"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:49
#: e340f70a70794fc6b8a18e795c87bd93
msgid ""
"There are two \"sides\" to the positive circuit in the board. Each side has "
"positive-rails available for inputing power or distributing it to peripheral"
" devices. The center row of pins in the three groups of pins (Outputs, "
"Inputs, Analog) labeled \"+\" are referred to as a \"positive-rail\". This "
"means that the base of all the + pins are connected so they represent a "
"single electrical path. The positive-rails of the Input and Analog group are"
" connected together. So we have two separate positive circuits, one in the "
"Outputs and the other made up of the Input/Analog."
msgstr ""
"电路板上的正极回路分为两「侧」。每侧均有可用于输入电源或向外围设备分配电源的正极排针。三组引脚（输出、输入、模拟）中间行标有「+」的引脚称为「正极排」，即所有"
" + 引脚的底部相互连接，形成单一电气通路。输入组和模拟组的正极排相互连通，因此共有两条独立的正极回路：一条在输出侧，另一条由输入/模拟侧共同构成。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:59
#: 8ac42662ca7b461284ac6394159d32d7
msgid ""
"All of the components on the board take power from various points on these "
"rails, so it is necessary for both \"sides\" to be receiving +5V (within the"
" specs below) for the board to function."
msgstr "板上所有元件均从这些排针的各个位置取电，因此两「侧」都必须接收 +5V（在下述规格范围内），电路板才能正常工作。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:63
#: 9e35e9b6887548f6828e14e8731cd984
msgid ""
"These positive-rails can be joined together by placing JP1 in its position "
"on the board. This connects all the positive-rails ands provides power to "
"both sides of the board, so that low-level power can be distributed to "
"peripheral sensors and devices: 3DR Radios, sonar, RC Rx, etc. via the "
"power-rails."
msgstr ""
"通过将 JP1 "
"安装到电路板上的对应位置，可将这些正极排连接在一起。这样可连通所有正极排，并为电路板两侧供电，使低级电源能够通过电源排向外围传感器和设备（3DR "
"无线电、声纳、RC 接收机等）分配。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:69
#: bad9b12713e04598a6f4945bd082847a
msgid "When using the power module, the circuit path is as follows:"
msgstr "使用电源模块时，电路路径如下："

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:71
#: a3e3e465d0fc41dd93035a39a19a94d1
msgid ""
"From the power module connection the negative wire is connected to a "
"negative-rail shared by the entire board regardless of JP1."
msgstr "从电源模块连接处，负线连接到无论 JP1 如何设置、全板共用的负极排。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:74
#: 8df38283a79b41078d00035e425a1511
msgid ""
"Positive voltage comes in to a T-junction. to the left is a path through the"
" JP1 to the positive-rail of the Outputs. To the right it flows through an "
"over-voltage, over-current, reverse-polarity protection(500mA fuse and 6V "
"Zener diode). A side effect of passing through the Zener diode is a .37V "
"loss, therefore input voltage should be bumped up by .37V to account for "
"this. From here the positive voltage runs to the positive-rails of the "
"Inputs and Analog. Inputs should not be used to power anything except your "
"RC receiver."
msgstr ""
"正电压进入一个 T 形接头。向左经过 JP1 到达输出侧正极排；向右则经过过压、过流、反极性保护（500mA 保险丝和 6V "
"稳压二极管）。通过稳压二极管时会损失 0.37V，因此输入电压应相应提高 0.37V "
"以补偿损耗。之后正电压流向输入和模拟的正极排。输入端除接收机外不应为其他设备供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:83
#: 67668b1a077e47c7816b236f88a086b7
msgid ""
"Higher current loads such as servos should be powered from the power-rails "
"(positive-negative) of the Output side. You must use an adequate voltage-"
"regulator to provide power directly to the Output power-rails, all servo "
"power leads will attach to these same rails (the signal wires can connect on"
" the Analog \"S\" pins in the case of a camera gimbal). Since JP1 is removed"
" in this scenario, the other \"side\" of the board will need power provided "
"to its power-rails directly."
msgstr ""
"较大电流负载（如舵机）应从输出侧电源排（正负极）取电。您必须使用足够的稳压器直接向输出电源排供电，所有舵机的电源线均连接到这些排针上（信号线可连接到模拟侧的「S」引脚，例如用于云台摄像头）。由于在此场景中"
" JP1 已拆除，电路板另「侧」需要直接向其电源排供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:92
#: 00bb8024c705471198542ae100e63c40
msgid "Alternative ways to power your board"
msgstr "为电路板供电的其他方式"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:94
#: a244037285ca4501b93b7c303a1b422a
msgid ""
"If you are using the 3DR Power Module please find instructions here: \\ "
":ref:`Using the 3DR Power Module <common-3dr-power-module>`"
msgstr ""
"如果您使用的是 3DR 电源模块，请在此处查阅说明：\\ :ref:`Using the 3DR Power Module <common-3dr-"
"power-module>`"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:99
#: d55839ffc97d46e8a6214f819a86052d
msgid ""
"Under no circumstances should you ever attempt to draw servo power from the "
"analog input connector."
msgstr "任何情况下都不得尝试从模拟输入连接器取用舵机电源。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:104
#: 7a1333bc2fdc4a44aaea5f55e757b6a5
msgid ""
"You may \"control\" servos from A9, A10 and A11 from the A0 - A11 I/O "
"connector, but you must run servo power separately."
msgstr "您可以从 A0–A11 I/O 连接器的 A9、A10 和 A11 「控制」舵机，但必须单独提供舵机电源。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:107
#: 8a654cd3303e43318125de3b3bd093e9
msgid "The A0 - A11 I/O connector cannot supply sufficient power for servos."
msgstr "A0–A11 I/O 连接器无法为舵机提供足够的电源。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:108
#: 34f236a419eb46c7a4a140a5e83346ea
msgid ""
"A9, A10 and A11 of the I/O connector come pre-wired to correct digital out "
"for use as servo control lines."
msgstr "I/O 连接器的 A9、A10 和 A11 已预先连接到正确的数字输出，可用作舵机控制线。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:110
#: 91e65e8c2f944e4dacb77abf619c3360
msgid ""
"For servo use, it is imperative that they have not been reassigned to analog"
" use with the pads on the back of the APM board."
msgstr "若用于舵机，必须确保这些引脚未通过 APM 板背面的焊盘被重新分配为模拟用途。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:114
#: 7534b1e9b45d46d8b277274ff2147b34
msgid "Non-technical description of the power supply requirements"
msgstr "电源需求的非技术性说明"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:116
#: abe3e1a19d694669be4d73abcf5a9996
msgid ""
"The description below simply supplements and provides an alternate view of "
"the information above."
msgstr "以下说明仅作为上述信息的补充，提供另一种理解视角。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:119
#: fd38fa67305044d3829f64b73ec3255e
msgid ""
"The APM 2.5/2.6 board has two separate power circuits which make it very "
"easy to power by a variety of methods."
msgstr "APM 2.5/2.6 电路板具有两条独立的供电回路，可通过多种方式方便地供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:122
#: 83b3f251c3794cb393ad07e81396213d
msgid ""
"A fused power circuit provides primary board and general I/O power: (It "
"cannot provide power for servos)."
msgstr "一条带保险丝的供电回路为电路板主体及通用 I/O 供电（无法为舵机供电）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:124
#: 7c524df9e4084636b70be399772fdc1c
msgid ""
"The Other power circuit is for the OUTPUT connector power rail: (it can "
"provide power for servos)."
msgstr "另一条供电回路用于输出连接器电源排（可为舵机供电）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:127
#: 10d0006bf1bc4dafbec71e0858b5e3be
msgid ""
"The jumper JP 1 determines whether the two power circuits are connected or "
"separate."
msgstr "跳线 JP1 决定两条供电回路是连通还是分离。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:130
#: bf1578bd91ce4c528373262ac41e8fb3
msgid ""
"If JP1 is removed, the power rail on the OUTPUT connector \"Floats\" and may"
" be used to distribute power."
msgstr "若拆除 JP1，输出连接器上的电源排将「悬空」，可用于分配电源。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:132
#: c6f8c27e7afc4ed5a6638bcc66b163dc
msgid ""
"Although if JP1 is removed the OUTPUT connector cannot be used to supply "
"power to the APM board."
msgstr "但若拆除 JP1，则不能通过输出连接器向 APM 电路板供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:135
#: 24d8ef875e674c5d8d46b203063dae73
msgid ""
"It is possible to power the APM board from the Power Module connector or the"
" OUTPUT or INPUT connectors."
msgstr "可通过电源模块连接器、输出连接器或输入连接器为 APM 电路板供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:137
#: 835d1c8d9000421caa6518dc6d6cbc90
msgid ""
"Normally the APM 2.5/2.6 \"Power Module\" is used to provide primary APM 2.5"
" board and general I/O power."
msgstr "通常使用 APM 2.5/2.6 「电源模块」为 APM 2.5 电路板及通用 I/O 提供主供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:139
#: 94b016e96085436a95f20aca9a118791
msgid ""
"Alternatively primary board power can be supplied by a BEC either from one "
"of the ESCs or from an external BEC."
msgstr "也可通过 ESC 自带的 BEC 或外接独立 BEC 为电路板提供主供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:141
#: eafe869afa8b408cba60e4d1eec11a33
msgid "If servos are used, supplementary power is required."
msgstr "如果使用了舵机，则需要补充供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:143
#: 8b72a40ba1724b65a4045b2f0a65122b
msgid ""
"Generally one power supply is provided for the board and one or more "
"additional power supplies for the servos."
msgstr "一般情况下，为电路板提供一路电源，再为舵机提供一路或多路附加电源。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:145
#: b3972c46ca18450794f70ff11da54845
msgid ""
"But if a sufficiently large external BEC is used it can supply power for "
"both via the OUTPUT connector."
msgstr "但如果使用了功率足够大的外接 BEC，也可通过输出连接器同时为两者供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:148
#: e0d016082cc14d90a39e8f3ba5d415db
msgid ""
"Only the OUTPUT connector can provide power for servos as the other circuit "
"is fused."
msgstr "只有输出连接器可为舵机供电，因为另一条回路带有保险丝。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:151
#: 917d083f8f3a47278a5d81431a18523c
msgid ""
"The address connector is sometimes used provide servo signals, but the "
"servos power must come from elsewhere."
msgstr "地址连接器有时用于提供舵机信号，但舵机电源必须另行提供。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:154
#: 9895f28b78794ee48b3be9a16e511bb1
msgid ""
"How you are powering your APM board and or servos determines whether JP1 is"
"  installed or not."
msgstr "您为 APM 电路板和/或舵机供电的方式决定了是否需要安装 JP1。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:157
#: 7ce24a05c4a14dea842cf9af7e2d2f83
msgid "(Whether the two power circuits are separated or connected)."
msgstr "（即两条供电回路是分离还是连通）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:158
#: 747f785cd1734a50bb1c9104fca93d69
msgid "All possible configurations are detailed Below."
msgstr "所有可能的配置详见下文。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:160
#: add42caeb7304906ae202187c70a6c81
msgid "The type of use will determine which options are available."
msgstr "使用类型将决定哪些选项可用。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:162
#: 03d4201a635342c9837e0742c20bde39
msgid ""
"Copter can power the APM from a power module or a UBEC or a BEC from one of "
"the ESCs and can power servos from a UBEC or from the other ESC's BECs."
msgstr ""
"Copter 可通过电源模块、UBEC 或某个 ESC 的 BEC 为 APM 供电，并可通过 UBEC 或其他 ESC 的 BEC 为舵机供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:165
#: f9d388f8a45140c5b212e6bf6e43126a
msgid ""
"Plane can power the APM from the power module,  the BEC from the flight "
"motors ESC or a  separate UBEC and can power servos from a separate UBEC or "
"the flight motors BEC if it is large enough."
msgstr ""
"Plane 可通过电源模块、飞行电机 ESC 的 BEC 或独立 UBEC 为 APM 供电，并可通过独立 UBEC 或飞行电机 "
"BEC（若功率足够）为舵机供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:168
#: 8aa1397aef754d15b9a54d09a0adb2de
msgid ""
"Rover  can power the APM from the power module,  the BEC from the drive "
"motor's ESC or a  separate UBEC and can power the steering servo from a "
"separate UBEC or the drive motors BEC if it is large enough."
msgstr ""
"Rover 可通过电源模块、驱动电机 ESC 的 BEC 或独立 UBEC 为 APM 供电，并可通过独立 UBEC 或驱动电机 "
"BEC（若功率足够）为转向舵机供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:174
#: e44683e99eda4b429e45859894feae3c
msgid "Power supply rails connected requirements (JP1 Installed)"
msgstr "电源排已连接的要求（JP1 已安装）"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:178
#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:270
#: 4686d752bc01444baae7787ce4324936 f5984a4e51604977a89c130d88913bfb
msgid ""
"Do not exceed Abs MAX input voltages when connecting the power supply or you"
" will damage your board."
msgstr "连接电源时请勿超过绝对最大输入电压，否则将损坏电路板。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:183
#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:275
#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:355
#: 2ec1d2849b5048179a795e4d88751a33 70371caefebe40f7a4724d1d2a154599
#: b200d91e49cf4975b4dfc0c4532d0552
msgid ""
"Connecting USB when you have input voltages at the high end of the range "
"(near Abs Max) can damage the board. Disconnect battery before connecting "
"USB or test input voltages so they are within the specified range."
msgstr "当输入电压处于范围高端（接近绝对最大值）时连接 USB 可能损坏电路板。连接 USB 前请先断开电池，或确认输入电压在规定范围内。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:189
#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:281
#: 81f4bcfa1c964428a73d9267f358c56a ef76ada0c3a147419e5b438ee4c48839
msgid "Power Options"
msgstr "供电选项"

#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:189
#: ../../source/docs/common-powering-the-apm2.rst:281
#: 57fd000068f346b4a175b75ade5fa504 59b015aa176c429a90ff3a86667cead2
msgid "Nominal"
msgstr "标称值"

